  "question": {
    "html": "<p>Two particles, <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"X\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"Y\"></span>, with the same electric charge enter a region of uniform magnetic field <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"B\"></span> with the same kinetic energy. The magnetic field is perpendicular to the initial velocity of the particles. The diagram shows the semi-circular paths of the particles within the field.</p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure></p>\n<p>The radius of the path for particle <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"Y\"></span> is twice the radius of the path for particle <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"X\"></span>. What is the ratio <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{\\text{mass of particle } Y}{\\text{mass of particle } X}\"></span>?</p><ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"0.25\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"B\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"0.50\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"C\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2.0\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"D\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"4.0\"></span></p></li></ol>"
